// P2: loop index that can exceed the array size.
// Array of size 3, n in [0, 5]; when n is 3, 4 or 5 the store a[i] runs with
// i = 3 or i = 4, so an out-of-bounds fault really occurs.  The analysis
// reports a possible upper-bound OOB at the store (line of a[i]), and the
// concrete interpreter faults for n >= 3.  This is an "exact" case: every
// alarm matches a real fault and every real fault is caught.
input n;
arr a[3] = [1, 2, 3];
var i = 0;
while (i < n) {
  a[i] = i;
  i = i + 1;
}
